    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600-a2">

                <pb facs="0674" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg594"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The committee of safety to
                        Mr. Powell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: It has come to the knowledge of
                    the committee of public safety, sitting at the capital, that following the
                    events that have unrolled in this city a certain <pb facs="0675" n="595"
                        xml:id="pg595"/> number of Haitian citizens have sought asylum in the
                    different legations and consulates.</p>
                <p>In consequence we would be greatly obliged to you to kindly, conformable to
                    precedents, transmit to this committee the list of names of those of our
                    citizens that may have taken refuge at the legation of the United States of
                    America in this city.</p>
                <p>With our thanks, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boisrond Canal</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">President of the Committee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
